# Phase Management

Phases in this workspace are named (Chronicle Phase 9, Phase 2F, Phase 17 proof, etc.). Do not invent a single global increment. Inspect existing `docs/**` phase reports before numbering.

## Start Phase X / next / NEXT

1. Inspect repo: `node scripts/dev-workflow/inspect-repo.mjs` plus `git status` / `git worktree list`
2. Protect unrelated dirty files; do not reset or stash
3. Read the previous phase closeout if it exists
4. Define goal, in scope, out of scope, acceptance criteria, risks, validation plan
5. Choose implementation owner (Cursor or Codex)
6. Choose branch/worktree only if isolation is needed
7. Stop at implementation readiness unless the user asked to implement

Do not begin broad implementation until those boundaries are written in the reply (use `docs/templates/phase-plan.md`).

## Continue Phase X

Stay inside the existing scope. Re-read acceptance criteria. Do not expand into neighboring systems.

## Close Phase X

A phase is complete only when acceptance is checked, relevant tests/builds have real results, the diff is reviewed, blockers are documented, Git state is understood, and checkpoints exist.

Closeout fields: PHASE, STATUS, SUMMARY, ACCEPTANCE RESULTS, TEST RESULTS, BUILD RESULTS, MANUAL QA, COMMITS, KNOWN LIMITATIONS, REMAINING BLOCKERS, NEXT RECOMMENDED PHASE.

Never mark a blocked phase complete. Template: `docs/templates/phase-closeout.md`.
